## When to document

- Always: Public and protected methods of services, repositories, controllers.
- Always: Public API methods and non-obvious parameters.
- Optional: Private methods only if the logic is complex.
- Always: Class summary for services, repositories, and key domain classes.

## Tags to use

- @param for every parameter (type and name, then description).
- @return for return type and brief description.
- @throws for every exception the method can throw.
- @see for related class or method when relevant.
- Use array<string, mixed> or list<int> for generic arrays when useful.
